#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092406 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092406 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of Equations Using Inverse Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092406 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186092995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092406 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092406 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "95d8fd9f-fddb-5a11-8670-194ad28cdab0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1061 16484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e9e60d9-ca5d-5380-9aad-e2eb767f920e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092996 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092996 #edb/ref 1061 16485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092996 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e317b6ac-3382-5ce2-962a-936c0a5dc928" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092996 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092997 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092997 #edb/ref 1061 16486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092997 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fbf465d4-96d6-52f9-879f-09f247f27b80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092997 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092999 #edb/ref 1061 16759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092999 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a3ebe3d-7f48-57e9-995c-5652343c5b4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092999 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093403 #edb/ref 1064 "We know that we can write a system of three linear equations in three variables in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n- $A$ is the $3\\times 3$ coefficient matrix,\n\n- $\\mathbf{x}$ is the column vector of variables, and\n\n- $\\mathbf{b}$ is the column vector of constants.\n\nIf the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ is invertible, then we can find a solution to the system $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ by \"pre-multiplying\" both sides of the equation by $A^{-1}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ {I}_{3}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ we simply calculate $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nLet's see how this works for a particular system in the next example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093403 #edb/ref 1065 3054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093403 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4c0fe954-2cf5-5eb6-b58f-c6963f5be7f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093403 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1080 "x=B\\,d\\,A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346254 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6788781d-31d5-5bd7-b27b-68afaa4d9325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1080 "x=B\\,d\\,{A}^{-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346708 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9bded5b5-b83d-570e-9629-cd29113e20b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1080 "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346783 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4a497d7-ea8a-5a5f-b4fd-1d8c483ff5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1080 "x=BA\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346945 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b6d2cc68-86a2-5604-8401-931a07c9e6b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1080 "x=AB\\,d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347347 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e304282a-e8e7-5d48-b8b7-fb2bbc3eab5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186347347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347921 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b4e01459-2873-55b9-8f7c-c4fb473002de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $7\\times 7$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $7\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f0cd9e3-58c9-5ff5-838e-38f22a6e88cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348099 #edb/ref 1074 "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x=B\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & =B\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ {I}_{7}\\,x & =AB\\,d \\\\ x & =AB\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1069 "q-78559" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,z=c.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $z$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $c$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & =c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and right to left, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "863bd08e-01cd-5a69-b3ce-bacc176f8b4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403947 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,z=c$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & ={D}^{-1}c \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and ${I}_{n}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403948 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4cf7d7a2-cf8f-5d79-a5a3-2c7fb6abb055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403949 #edb/ref 1080 "${D}^{-1}$ and ${I}_{n}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53d8f566-865b-5d1d-968f-ffc7aeaaf0b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403950 #edb/ref 1080 "$D$ and ${I}_{n}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403950 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403950 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6898f8cf-ef60-599d-b703-aeb35e14e141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403951 #edb/ref 1080 "${D}^{-1}$ and $D$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403951 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403951 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0329ed6f-dee9-5205-b238-18984ed73972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403952 #edb/ref 1080 "${D}^{-1}$ and ${D}^{-1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403952 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403952 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a15466de-3c65-5970-8e36-5b25e21ca209" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403953 #edb/ref 1080 "$D$ and $z$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403953 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "daabc2d4-f4ce-50f8-9f41-a9e7585ac6e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of Equations Using Inverse Matrices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186415691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415683 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "19f27baf-34c3-5e03-bcb6-d2509997eb57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415684 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415684 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415684 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415685 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=\\frac{9}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415685 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415685 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "854c87f7-583e-578a-92c5-d3db59792427" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415686 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=-9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415686 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415686 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "92176233-f61a-5a1f-a96a-0e59d129daf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415687 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-5,y=18,z=-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415687 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415687 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "922397fb-a6df-5cdc-b3c4-40ed001f749e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415688 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-5,y=-18,z=-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415688 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415688 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d2d344f8-2327-5d63-96e1-0bdf947cb05c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415689 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7180735-62b0-5917-9dd2-0f45d066402b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1069 "q-10091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415690 #edb/ref 1074 "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-1(1-9)+2(1-6) \\\\  & =+8-10 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 9 \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415691 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415691 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "100a637e-a49a-5d4a-80d2-e88a9e19ca4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415691 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415692 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "227ec066-022a-52e9-9829-1a29de29e8db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415692 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186348099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415693 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "42e8894e-d466-5fe7-9f98-3286e55d0c47" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186403947 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
